---
title: Operator invite lifecycle and expiry
description: Domain rule — workspace invites are time-bounded INVITED rows with terminal ACCEPTED / EXPIRED / REVOKED states; accept is join-only and lifecycle-gated.
---

# Operator invite lifecycle and expiry

```yaml
id: INVITE-LIFECYCLE-INVARIANT
version: "2026-08-20"
status: LOCKED
authority: invite-lifecycle.ts · users-rbac.policy.ts · invites.service.ts · identity repositories
decisions: [DEC-P9-015, DEC-P9-018]
related:
  - invite-accept-membership-invariant.mdoc
  - invite-active-uniqueness-invariant.mdoc
  - users-api-dispatch-addendum.md
```

## Current storage (pre-P1.2 baseline)

| Field | Type | Notes |
| ----- | ---- | ----- |
| `inviteId` | UUID PK | Stable audit id |
| `inviteToken` | UUID unique | Accept URL token |
| `tenantId` | UUID FK | Tenant scope |
| `phone` | text | Normalized on write |
| `role` | text | admin \| member \| viewer |
| `status` | text | Default **`INVITED`** (pending/active) |
| `nameNote` | text? | Optional owner note |
| `invitedByUserId` | UUID | Owner who sent invite |
| `createdAt` | timestamptz | Row creation |
| `expiresAt` | timestamptz | **Added P1.2** — hard accept deadline |

**Status vocabulary**

| Stored status | Meaning | Listed in `GET /users/invites` | Acceptable |
| ------------- | ------- | -------------------------------- | ---------- |
| `INVITED` | Pending / active (diagram: **PENDING**) | Yes, when `expiresAt > now` | Yes, when not expired |
| `ACCEPTED` | Consumed; membership created | No | No |
| `EXPIRED` | TTL elapsed; row retained | No | No |
| `REVOKED` | Owner revoked; row retained | No | No |

API responses keep **`status: "INVITED"`** for pending queue rows (no UI change). Terminal rows are omitted from the pending list.

**Migration:** required — add `expires_at` NOT NULL, backfill `created_at + 7 days` for existing `INVITED` rows.

## Lifecycle diagram

```text
                    create (POST /users/invite)
                              |
                              v
                         INVITED (pending)
                         expiresAt set
                    /        |         \
         accept OK    lazy TTL      owner DELETE
              |       on accept          |
              v           |              v
          ACCEPTED     EXPIRED       REVOKED
         (retained)   (retained)    (retained)
```

Rows are **not deleted** on accept/revoke/expiry (audit trail). P1.1 duplicate guard treats only **active** invites (`INVITED` + unexpired) as blocking.

## Expiry rules

- TTL default: **7 days** (`OPERATOR_INVITE_TTL_MS` env override; tests use explicit `expiresAt` on seeds).
- **Before expiry:** accept allowed (subject to P0 membership invariant).
- **After expiry:** accept rejected with **410** `INVITE_EXPIRED`; lazy transition `INVITED → EXPIRED` at accept boundary; no `UserTenant` write; invite row retained.

## Resend (Option B — chosen)

`POST /users/invites/{id}/resend` (R6):

- Dispatches login OTP only.
- **Does not** extend `expiresAt`.
- **Does not** rotate `inviteToken` (shared accept links stay valid until expiry/revoke/accept).
- Fails **404** when invite is not active (`EXPIRED` / `REVOKED` / `ACCEPTED` or past TTL).

Rationale: resend is an OTP nudge on the existing invite window, not a new invitation. Extending TTL on every resend would allow indefinite invites via repeated resend spam.

## Revoke

`DELETE /users/invites/{id}`:

- Sets `status = REVOKED` (row retained).
- Clears active-phone index (P1.1).
- Accept → **410** `INVITE_REVOKED`.
- New invite for same phone allowed (no active row).

## Accept security

| Terminal / invalid state | HTTP | Code | Side effects |
| ------------------------ | ---- | ---- | ------------ |
| Missing token | 404 | `INVITE_NOT_FOUND` | none |
| `EXPIRED` (or lazy-expired) | 410 | `INVITE_EXPIRED` | status → `EXPIRED` if was `INVITED` |
| `REVOKED` | 410 | `INVITE_REVOKED` | none |
| `ACCEPTED` | 410 | `INVITE_ALREADY_ACCEPTED` | none |
| Cross-tenant token | 403 | `INVITE_TENANT_MISMATCH` | none |
| Phone mismatch | 403 | `INVITE_PHONE_MISMATCH` | none |
| Existing membership (P0) | 403/409 | owner/member codes | none |

Tenant isolation unchanged: lifecycle evaluated per `(inviteToken → tenantId)`; expiry in workspace A does not affect workspace B.

## Sequence (accept)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant S as acceptWorkspaceInvite
  participant L as evaluateInviteLifecycleForAccept
  participant R as acceptPendingInvite
  S->>R: findInviteByToken (any status)
  alt missing
    S-->>S: INVITE_NOT_FOUND
  else lifecycle reject
    S->>L: status + expiresAt
    L-->>S: EXPIRED / REVOKED / ACCEPTED
  else allow
    S->>R: mark ACCEPTED + insert UserTenant
  end
```
